  "status": "MOCK scenarios over the ABSTRACT proof model; see the 0.3 file for call meanings. Not evidence about pocold or MPT proofs.",
  "precedence": [
    "After proof1 verifies: S1 state.slot2Bits (bits 64-255 of slot 2 non-zero); S2 state.countRange (versionCount > 1024); S3 state.currentRange (currentVersion > versionCount)",
    "Then selection: default with currentVersion 0 -> noSite; n > versionCount -> versionNotFound (no proof2)",
    "After proof2 verifies: V1 state.recordBits (bits 104-255 of base+1 non-zero); V2 state.recordAbsent (manifestLen 0, manifestHash 0 and chunk count 0 for an id <= versionCount); V3 state.statusDomain (status not in {0,1,2}); V4 state.publishedBlock (draft with publishedBlock != 0, or published/revoked with publishedBlock not in 1..N)",
    "Then outcome: default needs status 1 else state.currentNotPublished; explicit: 0 refuseDraft, 2 revokedInterstitial (zero frames until confirmed, U02), 1 render",
    "Every state.* outcome is stateInvariant: zero frames, no restart, no chunk fetch"
  ],
